      "description": "Hōkoku-ji (報国寺) is an old temple in the Kenchō-ji school of the Rinzai sect of Zen Buddhism located in Kamakura, Japan. Famous for its bamboo garden, it is also known as \"Bamboo Temple\".\nA statue of Gautama Buddha, called Shaka Nyorai in Japanese, in a sacred hall is the temple's principal image.",
